### === TASK 1: Layered Architecture & Basic Endpoints ===

### Get all rooms (200 OK)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/rooms
Accept: application/json

### Get existing room by ID (200 OK)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/rooms/1
Accept: application/json

### Get non-existing room by ID (Should return 404 NOT_FOUND)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/rooms/999
Accept: application/json

### Get all reservations (includes seeded historical reservation id=1, without internalNote)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Accept: application/json

### Get reservations filtered by roomId=1 (200 OK)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?roomId=1
Accept: application/json

### Get reservations filtered by non-existent roomId=999 (Should return empty array [])
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?roomId=999
Accept: application/json


### === TASK 2: Validation with Zod ===

### Validation Error: Multiple errors at once (invalid roomId type, short reservedBy, invalid participants, invalid endTime, and unrecognized field isAdmin)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": "1",
  "reservedBy": "  ab  ",
  "participants": -5,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "not-a-date",
  "isAdmin": true
}

### Validation Error: Invalid room ID parameter in URL (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR instead of 404)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/rooms/abc
Accept: application/json

### Validation Error: Invalid roomId query parameter (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?roomId=abc
Accept: application/json

### Validation Error: Missing timezone offset in ISO date (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00"
}


### === TASK 3: Global Error Handling & Request Logging ===

### Unknown route (Should return 404 NOT_FOUND in JSON format, not HTML)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/nope
Accept: application/json

### Malformed JSON payload (Should return 400 INVALID_JSON)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

"malformed-json-body"

### Request with custom X-Request-Id header (Echoed back in response header and error body)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/rooms/999
Accept: application/json
X-Request-Id: custom-req-id-001

### Unexpected server crash (Should return 500 INTERNAL_ERROR without leaking stack trace)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/debug/crash
Accept: application/json
X-Request-Id: crash-demo-500


### === TASK 4: Business Rules - Time Constraints, Capacity & Overlapping Reservations ===

### Business Rule Error: startTime in the past (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2025-01-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2025-01-10T12:00:00.000Z"
}

### Business Rule Error: endTime not after startTime (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### Business Rule Error: Duration shorter than 15 minutes (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T10:10:00.000Z"
}

### Business Rule Error: Duration longer than 8 hours (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T08:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T17:00:00.000Z"
}

### Business Rule Error: Room capacity exceeded (Should return 409 ROOM_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Piotr Wiśniewski",
  "participants": 40,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z"
}

### Base Reservation (id=2): Create valid reservation 10:00-12:00 in Room 1 (201 Created + Location header)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Jan Kowalski",
  "participants": 20,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 1: 12:00-13:00 in Room 1 -> OK (201 Created, adjacent interval at end)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Anna Nowak",
  "participants": 15,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T13:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 2: 08:00-10:00 in Room 1 -> OK (201 Created, adjacent interval at start)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Anna Nowak",
  "participants": 15,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T08:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 3: 11:00-13:00 in Room 1 -> 409 Conflict (ROOM_ALREADY_BOOKED, overlaps 11:00-12:00)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Tomasz Zieliński",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T11:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T13:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 4: 09:00-13:00 in Room 1 -> 409 Conflict (ROOM_ALREADY_BOOKED, encloses 10:00-12:00)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Tomasz Zieliński",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T09:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T13:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 5: 10:30-11:00 in Room 1 -> 409 Conflict (ROOM_ALREADY_BOOKED, inside 10:00-12:00)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Tomasz Zieliński",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:30:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T11:00:00.000Z"
}

### Overlap Case 6: 10:00-12:00 in Room 2 -> OK (201 Created, different room)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 2,
  "reservedBy": "Katarzyna Wiśniewska",
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z"
}


### === TASK 5: Cancellation State Machine & Response DTO ===

### Attempt to cancel reservation that has already started (Seeded id=1 -> 409 RESERVATION_ALREADY_STARTED)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/1/cancel
Accept: application/json

### Cancel future reservation (id=2, 10:00-12:00 in Room 1 -> 200 OK, sets status=CANCELLED and cancelledAt)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/2/cancel
Accept: application/json

### Idempotent second cancellation of reservation id=2 (200 OK, cancelledAt remains unchanged)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/2/cancel
Accept: application/json

### Overlap Case 7: 10:00-12:00 in Room 1 when existing reservation (id=2) is CANCELLED -> OK (201 Created)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "reservedBy": "Michał Lewandowski",
  "participants": 25,
  "startTime": "2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime": "2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z"
}

### Cancel non-existing reservation (Should return 404 NOT_FOUND)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/999/cancel
Accept: application/json


### === LAB 3 - TASK 2: Buildings, Knex & PostgreSQL Persistence ===

### Get all buildings (Should return 2 buildings from the seed)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/buildings
Accept: application/json

### Get existing building by ID
GET http://localhost:3000/api/buildings/1
Accept: application/json

### Get non-existing building (Should return 404 NOT_FOUND)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/buildings/999
Accept: application/json

### Create a new building (201 Created)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/buildings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Budynek C",
  "address": "ul. Warszawska 25, Kraków"
}

### Create a new room associated with Building A (201 Created)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "103",
  "capacity": 45
}

### Validation Error: Create room with missing buildingId (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "104",
  "capacity": 20
}

### Conflict Error: Create room with duplicate name in the same building (Should return 409 UNIQUE_VIOLATION)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buildingId": 1,
  "name": "101",
  "capacity": 50
}

### === LAB 3 - TASK 4: Pagination, Filtering & Sorting ===

### Combo 1: Just pagination and descending participants limit
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?page=1&limit=2&sort=-participants
Accept: application/json

### Combo 2: Filtering by Building and Status + sorting by startTime
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?buildingId=2&status=CONFIRMED&sort=startTime
Accept: application/json

### Combo 3: Overlapping dates filter (should fetch reservations touching Nov 2026)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?from=2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z&to=2026-11-30T23:59:59.000Z
Accept: application/json

### Combo 4: Out of bounds page (Should return 200 OK with empty data array)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?page=99&limit=10
Accept: application/json

### Validation Error: from >= to (Should return 400 VALIDATION_ERROR)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/reservations?from=2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z&to=2026-11-10T10:00:00.000Z
Accept: application/json


### === LAB 4 - TASK 1: Creating an account / Registration ===

### 1. Correct user registration
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "Jan.Kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo"
}

### 2. Attempt to register an email address that is already in use
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo"
}

### 3. Attempt to inject an unauthorized 'role' field to gain privileges
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "hacker@example.com",
  "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 4. Attempt to create an account with a password that is too short
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "krotkie@example.com",
  "password": "krotkie"
}


